// REGRESSION: heap corruption after a thrown event crosses an inner
// unmatched typed catch arm and propagates to an outer catch.
//
// Filed 2026-05-18 by app-team (singular gateway live e2e, scenarios
// 10 / 11b / wrong-owner).  Root cause: the MIR lowering of
// `try { ... } catch SomeEvent(e) { ... }` for the no-match dispatch
// path used `LoadLocal` (a snapshot, not a consume) of the hidden
// `error_local` slot, then called `_propagate_error` which emits a
// function-exit `CleanupHook`.  The hook saw `error_local` as still-
// owning and emitted a `DropValue` that called `drift_error_release`
// on the envelope -- but the SAME pointer was simultaneously wrapped
// into the returned `FnResult.Err` for the caller, who then called
// `drift_error_release` on the freed envelope.  Result: UAF read of
// the envelope's `event_fqn`/`params_json`/`context_json` fields plus
// a double `free()` of the envelope, surfacing as `malloc():
// unaligned tcache chunk detected` or `double free or corruption
// (fasttop)` -- variant depending on which malloc call hits the
// corrupted chunk first.  Fix in
// `lang/driftc/stage2/hir_to_mir.py::_visit_stmt_HTry`: emit
// `M.MoveOut` at the propagation site so `error_local` is consumed
// and the cleanup hook skips it.
//
// This carrier deliberately uses the smallest shape that exhibits
// the bug: two empty `pub error` types and no destructible locals
// inside the inner try.  The bug is independent of payload shape
// (variants, Strings, Int fields, or empty errors all crash equally
// pre-fix) and independent of any helper frame.
//
// Exit 0 = the inner unmatched typed-catch + outer binder-less catch
// runs without heap corruption.  Pre-fix the process aborts after
// returning from main; post-fix the process exits cleanly.

module main;

pub error A {}
pub error B {}

fn inner() -> Int {
	try { throw A(); } catch B(e) { return 999; }
}

fn main() nothrow -> Int {
	return try inner() catch { 0 };
}
